flag: maple{binaries_are_not_secret}
keyscheck the binary with a decompiler, you will found that it takes the user input and XOR with a 4 byte array. It takes the xor result and compare with a bigger array. If all the bytes are same, it is the flag we want to know.
So, since X ^ b ^ b &#x3D;&#x3D; X, we just xor to get the flag.
here is the solution
